1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,090
Hello, everyone.

2
00:00:04,470 --> 00:00:07,130
Welcome back to another lesson with us here at EnglishPod.

3
00:00:07,450 --> 00:00:07,890
My name is Marco.

4
00:00:08,230 --> 00:00:09,550
My name is Catherine and that's us.

5
00:00:09,890 --> 00:00:10,430
And that's us.

6
00:00:10,770 --> 00:00:16,650
And today we're going to talk about a very common situation when you're a couple, when you have a girlfriend.

7
00:00:16,650 --> 00:00:17,330
Honey, come on.

8
00:00:17,850 --> 00:00:18,850
I want to go.

9
00:00:19,470 --> 00:00:19,910
Are you?

10
00:00:20,080 --> 00:00:21,760
You are taking forever.

11
00:00:22,710 --> 00:00:22,990
All right.

12
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:23,850
Who takes long?

13
00:00:24,360 --> 00:00:26,800
Like do you take a long time to get ready, to get dressed?

14
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:27,110
Okay.

15
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:39,400
I take longer to get ready, but my boyfriend takes longer in general because he's like checking his email, playing video games, like just, you know, we call it lollygagging.

16
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:41,630
He's just like being kind of slow.

17
00:00:42,810 --> 00:00:43,690
I'm the opposite.

18
00:00:44,990 --> 00:00:48,010
I usually start getting ready later.

19
00:00:48,310 --> 00:00:57,030
Like if we have to leave at nine, I'll start getting ready at 830, but I'll be ready by nine because I take a shower real fast, get dressed, and I know what I'm going to wear and all my clothes are ready.

20
00:00:57,770 --> 00:01:02,890
On the other hand, my girlfriend takes forever to get ready and she's like, oh, and then, you know, the hair.

21
00:01:03,840 --> 00:01:07,320
Girls have makeup and tights and shoes.

22
00:01:07,320 --> 00:01:08,070
But this is what I understand.

23
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:13,000
If we're supposed to leave at nine, why don't you start getting ready before?

24
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Never underestimate women.

25
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:15,000
I don't know.

26
00:01:15,650 --> 00:01:16,000
Procrastination.

27
00:01:16,490 --> 00:01:17,790
Hey, it's not even about procrastination.

28
00:01:18,320 --> 00:01:19,950
Sometimes it just takes longer to look good than other times.

29
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:21,450
Right.

30
00:01:21,950 --> 00:01:25,790
Well, in this case, we're going to be looking at a lesson where it's the opposite.

31
00:01:26,090 --> 00:01:33,410
The husband is taking a long time to get ready and well, I don't think he has a very good fashion sense, right?

32
00:01:33,650 --> 00:01:34,130
He does not.

33
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:36,640
And we're going to learn what that phrase means in a minute here.

34
00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:41,690
But before we get going, I've got a couple of words to preview to help you understand what's going on in today's dialogue.

35
00:01:43,480 --> 00:01:43,960
Vocabulary preview.

36
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:45,480
All right.

37
00:01:45,730 --> 00:01:47,050
So, vocabulary preview.

38
00:01:47,210 --> 00:01:48,170
Today we have two words.

39
00:01:48,830 --> 00:01:51,930
The first one can be a noun or a verb, to iron.

40
00:01:52,670 --> 00:01:53,290
Or iron.

41
00:01:55,350 --> 00:01:58,550
So to iron basically means to...

42
00:01:59,320 --> 00:02:01,190
To get the wrinkles out of clothes.

43
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:02,560
And so we use this...

44
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:04,110
Iron is actually a metal.

45
00:02:04,860 --> 00:02:06,370
It's a very important metal.

46
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:10,190
And an iron is a machine that we plug in.

47
00:02:10,390 --> 00:02:15,210
We use it to get the wrinkles, the lines out of our shirts and our skirts and everything.

48
00:02:15,510 --> 00:02:18,770
So, it's actually a very important thing to make sure that you look nice and put together.

49
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:20,120
Right.

50
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:23,110
So, you use an iron to iron your shirt or to iron your skirt.

51
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:25,450
And then we have sandals.

52
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:26,900
My favorite type of shoe.

53
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:27,580
Mine too.

54
00:02:27,940 --> 00:02:28,320
Sandals.

55
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:31,260
I have a friend who used to say she had claustrophobic feet.

56
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:33,300
Her feet didn't like to be in closed spaces.

57
00:02:33,460 --> 00:02:34,940
So, she only wore sandals.

58
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:39,000
So these are open shoes, open toe shoes basically.

59
00:02:39,480 --> 00:02:40,960
You wear them at the beach.

60
00:02:40,960 --> 00:02:42,190
Or you wear them in the summer in general.

61
00:02:42,470 --> 00:02:43,530
I'm wearing sandals right now.

62
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:46,950
And you have different types of sandals like sandals and flip-flops, right?

63
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:52,000
Flip-flops I think they're called that because they sound like flip-flop, flip-flop when you walk.

64
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:53,690
Alright, so those are our two words today.

65
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:57,450
Let's listen to the dialogue for the first time and then we'll be back.

66
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:03,120
Honey, come on.

67
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:07,000
We're going to be late.

68
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:09,480
Honestly, you take longer getting ready than I do.

69
00:03:10,380 --> 00:03:12,660
I was drying my hair and ironing my shirt.

70
00:03:13,260 --> 00:03:14,480
Can you come here for a second?

71
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:15,140
I need your help.

72
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:16,760
What is it?

73
00:03:17,190 --> 00:03:18,750
Why are all these clothes on the bed?

74
00:03:19,410 --> 00:03:20,490
I don't know what to wear.

75
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:22,530
Okay, give me your opinion.

76
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:24,170
Do you like the way this looks?

77
00:03:24,760 --> 00:03:28,010
The striped short-sleeved shirt with this checkered sweater and my lucky sandals.

78
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:30,230
I like the cut and hemline of these shorts.

79
00:03:30,720 --> 00:03:31,870
So I think I'll wear these as well.

80
00:03:32,440 --> 00:03:32,950
Are you joking?

81
00:03:33,590 --> 00:03:34,790
What am I going to do with you?

82
00:03:35,430 --> 00:03:37,490
You're going to a dinner party, not to the beach.

83
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:42,120
Wear the shirt with the silk tie I bought you and those corduroy pants.

84
00:03:42,120 --> 00:03:43,840
It's chilly outside so you can wear this coat.

85
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:45,140
Thanks, honey.

86
00:03:45,640 --> 00:03:46,940
You have such great fashion sense.

87
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:49,120
Now what am I going to do with my hair?

88
00:03:54,190 --> 00:03:55,130
All right, we're back.

89
00:03:55,480 --> 00:04:00,310
So interesting, this husband sounded a lot like a famous president, I think.

90
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:02,610
He did, but we'll get to that in a minute.

91
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:12,690
Before we do talk about who this guy is, I think it'd be a great idea to talk about some of these clothing terms because they're very useful for when you want to go shopping and for when you're getting dressed.

92
00:04:15,640 --> 00:04:15,930
Language takeaway.

93
00:04:18,760 --> 00:04:22,320
Okay, so the first word that we have on language takeaway is striped.

94
00:04:22,970 --> 00:04:27,090
All right, you might have heard of the American flag called stars and stripes.

95
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:33,530
Stripes are those lines on clothing or on flags that go up or down or left and right.

96
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:35,040
Exactly.

97
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:39,510
So if you have a striped shirt, you have many lines on your shirt that are going up and down or left and right.

98
00:04:39,770 --> 00:04:46,170
Right, and they say with fashion, lines that go left to right make you look fatter and lines that go up and down make you look thinner.

99
00:04:47,050 --> 00:04:47,710
And taller.

100
00:04:47,880 --> 00:04:48,880
And taller.

101
00:04:48,880 --> 00:04:49,880
Very good.

102
00:04:49,880 --> 00:04:55,150
And now moving on, if it's summer and you want to wear a shirt, you can wear a short sleeved shirt.

103
00:04:55,690 --> 00:04:56,630
All right, this is important.

104
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:02,300
So most people like to wear short sleeved shirts in the summertime because they're cooler.

105
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:05,640
And in the wintertime, that means we like to wear long sleeved shirts.

106
00:05:05,640 --> 00:05:09,000
Okay, so the sleeves are basically the arms of the shirt.

107
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:10,000
Exactly.

108
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:10,690
You say short sleeved.

109
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:13,000
Very good.

110
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:16,720
And then we have a checkered shirt or a checkered sweater in this case.

111
00:05:16,940 --> 00:05:24,720
Okay, so checkered means there are little squares on the shirt and usually one square is one color and the next square is another color.

112
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:26,440
So it looks like a checkerboard.

113
00:05:26,640 --> 00:05:27,380
Very good.

114
00:05:27,440 --> 00:05:28,440
That game, you know, checkers.

115
00:05:28,440 --> 00:05:29,720
Or like a chessboard.

116
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:30,720
Exactly.

117
00:05:30,720 --> 00:05:37,590
And so in this case, we've got a guy who's trying to wear a striped shirt and a checkered sweater.

118
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:40,160
That does not go well together, right?

119
00:05:40,160 --> 00:05:41,160
No.

120
00:05:41,160 --> 00:05:42,350
Too much stuff happening.

121
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:43,310
It's too busy.

122
00:05:43,920 --> 00:05:44,920
Too busy.

123
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:45,920
All right.

124
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:52,630
And not only that, but he wanted to wear shorts because he liked the cut and the hemline.

125
00:05:53,130 --> 00:06:00,210
Okay, these are actually terms that we normally use with women's clothing because you could say, I like the cut of this dress.

126
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:02,560
I like the shape that it has.

127
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:03,560
Very good.

128
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:15,080
So the hemline is the bottom of your skirt or your trousers or your shorts and hemline, we could say, my mother used to say this to me, the hemline is much too high, much too short.

129
00:06:15,080 --> 00:06:16,080
That skirt is not appropriate.

130
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:17,080
Yeah.

131
00:06:17,080 --> 00:06:18,500
So it's nice to have a hemline at the knee.

132
00:06:19,500 --> 00:06:20,240
All right.

133
00:06:20,520 --> 00:06:28,180
So the cut is the shape that the piece of clothing has like pants or skirts and the hemline would be the place where it ends, right?

134
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:30,400
The skirt, for example.

135
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:33,040
Like it pretty much tells you the length of something.

136
00:06:33,040 --> 00:06:33,320
Very good.

137
00:06:37,080 --> 00:06:40,420
And now the wife steps in, she's like, no, no, you're not wearing this.

138
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:46,800
She's telling him that she has to wear nice clothes and among those items is a silk tie.

139
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:47,480
Okay.

140
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:49,320
So a classic Father's Day gift.

141
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:50,920
Silk tie.

142
00:06:50,920 --> 00:06:51,660
I've given this one a couple of times.

143
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:57,200
A silk tie is a necktie, a long necktie that's made of silk.

144
00:06:57,200 --> 00:06:58,920
Silk is a very soft material, right?

145
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:00,360
Very expensive as well.

146
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:01,820
It can be, especially Italian silk.

147
00:07:03,080 --> 00:07:05,480
And I've always actually wanted to have silk sheets.

148
00:07:06,260 --> 00:07:07,120
Ooh, see, I don't know.

149
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:09,320
I feel like they would get very warm in the summer.

150
00:07:09,560 --> 00:07:10,560
Yeah.

151
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:13,040
Well, in the winter it would be awesome, but probably very cold in the winter as well.

152
00:07:13,240 --> 00:07:14,240
Yeah.

153
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:15,240
I don't know.

154
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:17,000
Well, it's one of those things.

155
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,980
And then she's also telling him to wear some corduroy pants.

156
00:07:20,490 --> 00:07:20,810
Okay.

157
00:07:20,810 --> 00:07:28,310
So it sounds like this might be a winter dialogue because corduroy is not something you wear in the summer because it's very heavy and thick.

158
00:07:29,190 --> 00:07:36,440
Corduroy actually is a fabric that usually has these kind of ribs or ridges.

159
00:07:36,660 --> 00:07:41,240
And so there's like little lines in the fabric that make it quite thick and rough when you...

160
00:07:41,320 --> 00:07:45,980
Almost not rough, but they make it feel very unique when you touch it.

161
00:07:46,200 --> 00:07:47,200
Yeah.

162
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:48,200
It's not smooth.

163
00:07:48,200 --> 00:07:49,200
It's a little bit rough, the fabric.

164
00:07:50,200 --> 00:07:51,200
Very good.

165
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:54,290
So those are all the clothing items that we've looked at today.

166
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:55,210
There's a lot of them.

167
00:07:55,640 --> 00:08:03,990
And obviously we'll post a couple of pictures on the site so you can see better what a silk tie looks like or especially corduroy pants.

168
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:04,570
Corduroy, yeah.

169
00:08:05,280 --> 00:08:06,280
All right.

170
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:07,610
So let's listen to this dialogue again.

171
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:11,650
We're going to slow it down a little bit and then we'll come back and look at some of the phrases.

172
00:08:17,130 --> 00:08:17,770
Honey, come on.

173
00:08:18,090 --> 00:08:18,730
We're going to be late.

174
00:08:19,390 --> 00:08:21,190
Honestly, you take longer getting ready than I do.

175
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:24,380
I was drying my hair and ironing my shirt.

176
00:08:24,900 --> 00:08:25,940
Can you come here for a sec?

177
00:08:26,280 --> 00:08:26,880
I need your help.

178
00:08:27,300 --> 00:08:28,000
What is it?

179
00:08:28,520 --> 00:08:30,000
Why are all these clothes on the bed?

180
00:08:30,460 --> 00:08:31,540
I don't know what to wear.

181
00:08:32,120 --> 00:08:33,560
Okay, give me your opinion.

182
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:35,200
Do you like the way this looks?

183
00:08:35,700 --> 00:08:39,060
The striped short-sleeve shirt with this checkered sweater, my lucky sandals.

184
00:08:39,300 --> 00:08:42,980
I like the cut and hemline of these shorts, so I think I'll wear these as well.

185
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:44,120
Are you joking?

186
00:08:44,820 --> 00:08:45,940
What am I going to do with you?

187
00:08:46,540 --> 00:08:48,660
We are going to a dinner party, not to the beach.

188
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:52,400
Wear this shirt with the silk tie I bought you and these corduroy pants.

189
00:08:53,160 --> 00:08:54,960
It's chilly outside, so you can wear this coat.

190
00:08:55,600 --> 00:08:56,260
Thanks, honey.

191
00:08:56,780 --> 00:08:58,080
You have such great fashion sense.

192
00:08:58,600 --> 00:09:00,260
Now, what am I going to do with my hair?

193
00:09:03,990 --> 00:09:07,390
Alright, we're back, so now let's start with Fluency Builder.

194
00:09:09,160 --> 00:09:09,410
Fluency Builder.

195
00:09:10,160 --> 00:09:13,440
OK, these are classic couple phrases, right?

196
00:09:13,440 --> 00:09:23,410
These are phrases you hear among couples, and the first one is maybe more common to hear from the female end, but it's not unknown on the male end.

197
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:24,670
So, we have this question.

198
00:09:25,640 --> 00:09:27,050
Do you like the way this looks?

199
00:09:27,760 --> 00:09:33,050
So while the person is saying this, they would maybe be moving to the side a little bit.

200
00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:34,390
Modeling it.

201
00:09:35,230 --> 00:09:36,390
Do you like the way this looks?

202
00:09:37,050 --> 00:09:40,270
So basically you're saying, do you like what I'm wearing?

203
00:09:40,550 --> 00:09:41,450
Does it look good on me?

204
00:09:41,490 --> 00:09:41,990
Does it look good?

205
00:09:42,600 --> 00:09:43,600
Exactly.

206
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:48,200
You could also say, hey, I like the way this looks when you're trying to buy something at the store.

207
00:09:48,200 --> 00:09:53,510
And so, do you like the way this looks is a way for you to ask the other person's opinion of how you look.

208
00:09:53,850 --> 00:10:02,510
And also, another common phrase, especially with men who have no fashion sense, the wife says, what am I going to do with you?

209
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:13,920
OK, this is an interesting phrase and it needs some explanation, I think, because the meaning is, well, this is very difficult, right?

210
00:10:13,960 --> 00:10:17,500
So you're being difficult or, wow, you need some help from me.

211
00:10:17,640 --> 00:10:18,260
I'm going to help you.

212
00:10:18,340 --> 00:10:21,960
How am I going to help you this much or all the time like this?

213
00:10:22,280 --> 00:10:26,280
Right, because she's pretty much saying he has no idea about clothing and fashion.

214
00:10:26,680 --> 00:10:31,760
So he's saying to her, what am I going to do with you?

215
00:10:31,880 --> 00:10:34,480
It means you need so much help.

216
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:34,800
Seriously.

217
00:10:35,720 --> 00:10:36,020
All right.

218
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:43,300
And the third phrase that we saw and we said at the very beginning is fashion sense.

219
00:10:43,560 --> 00:10:47,240
OK, so this is actually what the man needs help with.

220
00:10:47,240 --> 00:10:50,580
He needs help with his fashion sense because he has zero fashion sense.

221
00:10:51,200 --> 00:10:57,510
And this is pretty much a way to say how much someone knows about fashion or appearances.

222
00:10:58,040 --> 00:11:02,840
And so I can say, oh, my friend Kathy, she has amazing fashion sense.

223
00:11:02,890 --> 00:11:03,810
So she always looks good.

224
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:05,040
Right.

225
00:11:05,040 --> 00:11:11,680
So combining colors appropriately or wearing the right types of shoes with the right types of clothing, et cetera, fashion sense.

226
00:11:11,680 --> 00:11:16,710
Or even just being able to wear things that are good on her or telling other people what's good on them.

227
00:11:17,640 --> 00:11:23,250
So fashion sense is the ability to identify fashion and look good and make other people look good.

228
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:24,920
All right.

229
00:11:24,920 --> 00:11:25,920
Very good.

230
00:11:25,920 --> 00:11:32,330
Let's listen to this dialogue for the very last time and we'll come back and talk a little bit more about fashion because it's a very interesting topic.

231
00:11:34,880 --> 00:11:38,160
It is.

232
00:11:38,160 --> 00:11:42,240
Honey, come on.

233
00:11:42,240 --> 00:11:42,790
We're going to be late.

234
00:11:43,490 --> 00:11:45,290
Honestly, you take longer getting ready than I do.

235
00:11:45,970 --> 00:11:48,470
I was drying my hair and ironing my shirt.

236
00:11:48,990 --> 00:11:50,030
Can you come here for a sec?

237
00:11:50,350 --> 00:11:50,950
I need your help.

238
00:11:51,750 --> 00:11:52,550
What is it?

239
00:11:53,070 --> 00:11:54,550
Why are all these clothes on the bed?

240
00:11:55,090 --> 00:11:56,290
I don't know what to wear.

241
00:11:56,720 --> 00:11:58,520
OK, give me your opinion.

242
00:11:58,930 --> 00:11:59,950
Do you like the way this looks?

243
00:12:00,470 --> 00:12:03,810
The striped short sleeve shirt with this checkered sweater, my lucky sandals.

244
00:12:04,030 --> 00:12:06,050
I like the cut and hemline of these shorts.

245
00:12:06,270 --> 00:12:07,690
So I think I'll wear these as well.

246
00:12:08,090 --> 00:12:08,710
Are you joking?

247
00:12:09,370 --> 00:12:10,590
What am I going to do with you?

248
00:12:11,400 --> 00:12:14,400
We're going to a dinner party, not to the beach.

249
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:17,880
Wear the shirt with the silk tie I bought you and these corduroy pants.

250
00:12:17,880 --> 00:12:19,630
It's chilly outside so you can wear this coat.

251
00:12:20,330 --> 00:12:20,930
Thanks, honey.

252
00:12:21,430 --> 00:12:22,730
You have such great fashion sense.

253
00:12:23,250 --> 00:12:24,910
Now, what am I going to do with my hair?

254
00:12:31,570 --> 00:12:32,550
All right, we're back.

255
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:34,250
You lived in Italy for a while.

256
00:12:34,480 --> 00:12:35,950
How is the fashion over there?

257
00:12:36,040 --> 00:12:38,320
Is it extreme like we see on the runways?

258
00:12:38,320 --> 00:12:40,310
Because I honestly don't understand fashion.

259
00:12:41,070 --> 00:12:43,750
Well, the thing about runways is that that's not how normal people dress.

260
00:12:43,910 --> 00:12:45,250
Well, yeah, that's what I understand.

261
00:12:45,530 --> 00:12:49,310
Why do they have these fashion shows if people don't really buy these types of clothing?

262
00:12:49,710 --> 00:13:01,250
Well, sometimes people like stores, for example, big stores, department stores will buy fashions off of the runway and they'll kind of change them a little bit so that they're more appropriate for normal consumption.

263
00:13:01,250 --> 00:13:03,570
That means for normal people who want to wear them.

264
00:13:04,410 --> 00:13:13,430
But the runway fashions are actually, they're kind of like exaggerations of trends that will happen in the shopping world, right, in the commercial world.

265
00:13:13,640 --> 00:13:19,320
So the things that you see are like big, blown up exaggerations.

266
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:23,650
And we take bits and pieces of those in our daily lives to dress up.

267
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:28,960
So different colors or fabrics or like oftentimes you see kind of military outfits.

268
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:33,840
And so that will translate into military jackets that are very popular one season.

269
00:13:33,840 --> 00:13:38,490
And so Italy definitely counts as a very fashionable country, but it's not crazy.

270
00:13:38,980 --> 00:13:44,960
Well, every once in a while you see some more crazy clothes, but I think Japan is much more crazy as far as style.

271
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:45,960
Yeah, actually, yeah.

272
00:13:45,960 --> 00:13:54,290
Asian countries such as Japan or South Korea, they have very, also unique fashion as well, but it's very extreme to a certain point.

273
00:13:54,560 --> 00:13:59,760
And the color combinations they do is like red sneakers with green pants and like a blue jacket.

274
00:13:59,760 --> 00:14:00,210
It's very crazy.

275
00:14:00,760 --> 00:14:01,760
Right.

276
00:14:01,760 --> 00:14:02,760
And very bright.

277
00:14:02,760 --> 00:14:05,130
And you often see these shoes, you know, we call them platform shoes.

278
00:14:06,080 --> 00:14:07,590
It's kind of like you're standing on a brick.

279
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:09,560
Yeah, they're huge.

280
00:14:09,560 --> 00:14:12,360
And they're, you know, they're seven inches tall.

281
00:14:12,360 --> 00:14:14,010
And you see these little girls wearing these big shoes.

282
00:14:14,210 --> 00:14:17,390
And I just, I'm so scared when I see them because I feel like they're going to fall over.

283
00:14:17,830 --> 00:14:20,010
The other thing is that fashion is so expensive.

284
00:14:20,010 --> 00:14:28,560
If you actually want to buy something that's in like an authentic, I don't know, Carolina Herrera or Oscar de la Renta or something like that.

285
00:14:28,700 --> 00:14:29,420
It's so expensive.

286
00:14:30,060 --> 00:14:30,300
It is.

287
00:14:30,420 --> 00:14:31,620
But you know, high fashion is expensive.

288
00:14:33,760 --> 00:14:34,960
Fashion is not, doesn't have to be.

289
00:14:35,120 --> 00:14:42,260
You can be fashionable just looking at different stores and going to secondhand shops and making your own clothes.

290
00:14:42,640 --> 00:14:46,720
I mean, it's all about a sense of personal style and dressing yourself to be unique.

291
00:14:46,720 --> 00:14:47,760
Or you can get it at the fake market.

292
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:49,080
Or you can go to the fake market.

293
00:14:49,380 --> 00:14:49,560
Exactly.

294
00:14:50,960 --> 00:14:51,960
All right.

295
00:14:51,960 --> 00:14:52,960
That's all the time we have for today, guys.

296
00:14:52,960 --> 00:14:54,640
I hope you enjoyed this lesson.

297
00:14:54,640 --> 00:14:58,160
Please come to our website and comment at EnglishPod.com.

298
00:14:58,160 --> 00:15:02,060
And if you have any other suggestions or maybe your own pictures of crazy fashion, you can post.

299
00:15:02,640 --> 00:15:03,360
We're glad to see them.

300
00:15:03,640 --> 00:15:04,600
So we'll see you guys there.

301
00:15:04,840 --> 00:15:05,840
Yeah.

302
00:15:05,840 --> 00:15:06,600
As Marco said, hope to see you on the website.

303
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:07,760
That's about it for today.

304
00:15:08,120 --> 00:15:08,860
So goodbye, everyone.

305
00:15:09,120 --> 00:15:17,995
Bye.
